# Hands-on 4

## Difference between JPA, Hibernate and Spring Data JPA

### JPA

- Java Persistence API
- Specification (JSR 338)
- Defines persistence standards
- Does not provide implementation

---

### Hibernate

- ORM Framework
- Implements JPA
- Generates SQL automatically
- Maps Java Objects to Database Tables

---

### Spring Data JPA

- Built on top of JPA and Hibernate
- Reduces boilerplate code
- Provides built-in CRUD methods
- Automatically manages transactions

---

## Comparison

| Feature | JPA | Hibernate | Spring Data JPA |
|----------|-----|-----------|-----------------|
| Type | Specification | ORM Framework | Abstraction Layer |
| Implementation | No | Yes | Uses Hibernate |
| CRUD Operations | No | Yes | Yes |
| Transaction Management | No | Manual | Automatic |
| Boilerplate Code | High | Medium | Very Low |

---

